; viveka-min: the comparative that selects the lesser value.
; "lighter", "slower", "smaller", "shorter" etc. all express this:
; given two values of the same concept, find the one that is lesser.
; 
; viveka = discernment. min = the lesser side of the discernment.
; the proof graph holds both — viveka-min names the direction.
; 
; when this word appears in a question with two entities, the pipeline
; dispatches to viveka-ganana with direction="min".

(kosha viveka-min
  (vishesa logic-varga)
  (swarupa viveka)
  (abheda min)
  (yukta comparison inference))
